# Line endings for this repository, independent of the host's core.autocrlf.
# Git stores LF in the repository; eol=lf keeps the working tree LF too.
#
# Why it matters here: .gitignore arrived as CRLF in the working tree while the
# repository holds LF, so every `git status` showed it as modified and a plain
# `git add` would have rewritten all 33 lines instead of adding two. The
# container's .env/.gitattributes already covered *.bat/*.sh the same way.
.gitignore    text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf
